// The privileged-action record — the andara.audit.v1 topic.
//
// AW-SRV-008 writes the first one: every Admin RPC, every authorize rejection,
// every invite issued or redeemed, every refresh token revoked. AW-SRV-013 adds
// the content-publish fields (pack, version, override, reason) additively;
// numbers from 20 up are theirs.
//
// Keyed by actor_account_id, so one operator's history is one partition. The
// partition's order is the order the records were appended, which is not a
// guarantee of the order the actions committed in: two concurrent writes by one
// actor can append in either order, and a record whose append outlives
// AuditWriteTimeout lands after later ones. ts_unix_nano is when the record was
// made, after the action committed. A reader reconstructing a sequence of
// concurrent actions orders by the state each action changed, not by offset
// (AW-SRV-040, 2026-10-09). Retention is 365 days (deploy/kafka/topics.yaml):
// this is the record of who did what with operator authority, and long
